<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Math Derivations and Intuitions</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Mean-field Dynamics of Fokker-Planck Equation for Stochastic Kuramoto Models</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the thermodynamic limit of infinite oscillators (<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>), the collective dynamics of the oscillator population can be effectively described by the mean-field evolution of a single representative oscillator with phase variable <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. The corresponding probability density <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\theta,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\theta,t)</annotation></semantics></math> evolves according to the Fokker–Planck equation:</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial p(\theta,t)}{\partial t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial p(\theta,t)}{\partial t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}\Big[\big(K(t)r(t)\sin(\psi(t)-\theta)+K_{\text{ref}}(t)\sin(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta)\big)p(\theta,t)\Big]+D_{t}\frac{\partial^{2}p(\theta,t)}{\partial\theta^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}\Big[\big(K(t)r(t)\sin(\psi(t)-\theta)+K_{\text{ref}}(t)\sin(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta)\big)p(\theta,t)\Big]+D_{t}\frac{\partial^{2}p(\theta,t)}{\partial\theta^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(t)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the magnitude and phase of the complex order parameter, respectively. In the long-time limit, the quasi-equilibrium satisfies <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial p_{\text{st}}(\theta)/\partial t\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>st</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial p_{\text{st}}(\theta)/\partial t\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math>. At this point, the stationary solution <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\theta,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\theta,T)</annotation></semantics></math> approximately follows:</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E14X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{T}\frac{\partial^{2}p(\theta,T)}{\partial\theta^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{T}\frac{\partial^{2}p(\theta,T)}{\partial\theta^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}\Big[\big(K(T)r(T)\sin(\psi(T)-\theta)+K_{\text{ref}}(T)\sin(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta)\big)p(\theta,T)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo mathsize="1.600em">,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{\partial}{\partial\theta}\Big[\big(K(T)r(T)\sin(\psi(T)-\theta)+K_{\text{ref}}(T)\sin(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta)\big)p(\theta,T)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E14Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{T}\frac{\partial p(\theta,T)}{\partial\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{T}\frac{\partial p(\theta,T)}{\partial\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\big(K(T)r(T)\sin(\psi-\theta)+K_{\text{ref}}(T)\sin(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta)\big)p(\theta,T)+C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\big(K(T)r(T)\sin(\psi-\theta)+K_{\text{ref}}(T)\sin(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta)\big)p(\theta,T)+C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E14Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{p(\theta,T)}\frac{\partial p(\theta,T)}{\partial\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{p(\theta,T)}\frac{\partial p(\theta,T)}{\partial\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{K(T)r(T)\sin(\psi(T)-\theta)+K_{\text{ref}}(T)\sin(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta)}{D_{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{K(T)r(T)\sin(\psi(T)-\theta)+K_{\text{ref}}(T)\sin(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta)}{D_{T}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E14Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p(\theta,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p(\theta,T)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{K(T)r(T)}{D_{T}}\cos(\psi(T)-\theta)+\frac{K_{\text{ref}}(T)}{D_{T}}\cos(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta)+C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{K(T)r(T)}{D_{T}}\cos(\psi(T)-\theta)+\frac{K_{\text{ref}}(T)}{D_{T}}\cos(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta)+C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E14Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\theta,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\theta,T)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14Xd.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{Z}\exp(\frac{K(T)r(T)}{D_{T}}\cos(\psi(T)-\theta)+\frac{K_{\text{ref}}(T)}{D_{T}}\cos(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{Z}\exp(\frac{K(T)r(T)}{D_{T}}\cos(\psi(T)-\theta)+\frac{K_{\text{ref}}(T)}{D_{T}}\cos(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are constants, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalization constant. We assume <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math> because the distribution is periodic, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is absorbed into <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the average phase <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(T)</annotation></semantics></math> will synchronize to the reference <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the quasi-stationary solution is given by:</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\quad p_{\text{st}}(\theta)\approx\frac{1}{Z}\exp\left(\frac{K(T)r(T)+K_{\text{ref}}(T)}{D_{T}}\cos(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>st</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\quad p_{\text{st}}(\theta)\approx\frac{1}{Z}\exp\left(\frac{K(T)r(T)+K_{\text{ref}}(T)}{D_{T}}\cos(\psi_{\text{ref}}-\theta)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">This final form follows a von Mises distribution, reflecting the low-entropy steady state induced by synchronized interactions and reference phase attraction.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Local Score Matching</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At any timestep <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> of the Markov chain, the marginal distribution <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int p({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})p({\bm{\theta}}_{t}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\mathop{d{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int p({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})p({\bm{\theta}}_{t}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\mathop{d{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E16Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int p({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}p({\bm{\theta}}_{t}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\mathop{d{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int p({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}p({\bm{\theta}}_{t}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\mathop{d{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For any score <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})=\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})/p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})=\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})/p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we can rewrite the above equation leveraging this identity:</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E17X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int p({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})p({\bm{\theta}}_{t}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\mathop{d{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int p({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})p({\bm{\theta}}_{t}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\mathop{d{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E17Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cancel{p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})}\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="updiagonalstrike"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></menclose><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cancel{p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})}\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\cancel{p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})}p({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t})\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\mathop{d{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><menclose notation="updiagonalstrike"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></menclose><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\cancel{p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})}p({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t})\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\mathop{d{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E17Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}\sim p({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t})}\Big[\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}\sim p({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t})}\Big[\nabla_{{\bm{\theta}}_{t}}\log p({\bm{\theta}}_{t}|{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1})\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The above results indicate that the score can be effectively approximated by the local transition kernel.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Fourier Interpretation of Kuramoto Coupling</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From a spectral standpoint, local phase coupling behaves like an angular low<span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>pass filter. In the small<span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>angle approximation (<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sin({\bm{\theta}}_{j}-{\bm{\theta}}_{i})\approx{\bm{\theta}}_{j}-{\bm{\theta}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sin({\bm{\theta}}_{j}-{\bm{\theta}}_{i})\approx{\bm{\theta}}_{j}-{\bm{\theta}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) and without a global reference phase, the forward SDE reduces to a stochastic heat equation (or a graph Laplacian form equivalently):</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d{\bm{\theta}}^{i}_{t}}{dt}=K(t)\nabla^{2}{\bm{\theta}}_{t}^{i}+\sqrt{2D_{t}}\xi^{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d{\bm{\theta}}^{i}_{t}}{dt}=K(t)\nabla^{2}{\bm{\theta}}_{t}^{i}+\sqrt{2D_{t}}\xi^{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Laplacian operator. Each Fourier component decays like <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-K(t)k^{2}t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-K(t)k^{2}t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the spatial frequency. Modes with very high spatial frequency <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> (pixel<span id="A1.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>scale noise) are damped almost instantly, while moderate<span id="A1.SS3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>frequency modes (coherent, edge<span id="A1.SS3.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>defining structures) decay much more slowly. Consequently, the Kuramoto drift effectively filters away pixel<span id="A1.SS3.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>scale noise while preserving the smooth, orientation<span id="A1.SS3.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text">-</span>rich patterns that constitute edges.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Why Kuramoto Diffusion Falls Short on General Natural Images</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our Kuramoto coupling is foremost a synchronization mechanism: it excels at pulling similar phases together, thereby preserving edges and repetitive patterns. On orientation<span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>rich data where the data are dominated by the <span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">simple outlines and repeating ridge structures</span>, this yields sharp samples in fewer steps. By contrast, natural images (<em id="A1.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">e.g.,</em> CIFAR<span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>10) demand modeling <em id="A1.SS4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">e.g.,</em><span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> complex, global semantics (object shapes, color gradients, backgrounds), often characterized by higher-order and longer-range correlations</span>. In this setting, the local synchronization bias becomes less relevant and potentially even detrimental; an isotropic diffusion process with a global drift may be better suited to capture these large<span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text">-</span>scale, non<span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text">-</span>repetitive features. As a result, our method trades some global fidelity (reflected in higher CIFAR<span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text">-</span>10 FID) in exchange for strong local coherence.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>More Experimental Results</h2>

<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Inference algorithm for Kuramoto orientation diffusion models.</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
            
            
           Trained score network <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, noise variance schedule <math id="alg2.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{2D_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{2D_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, forward Kuramoto drift <math id="alg2.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{f}}(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{f}}(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, noise <math id="alg2.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
           Sample initial phase: <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}_{T}\sim p({\bm{\theta}}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}_{T}\sim p({\bm{\theta}}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
           Initialize timestep counter <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
            Update: <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}={\bm{\theta}}_{t}-{\bm{f}}({\bm{\theta}}_{t},t)+2D_{t}\cdot s({\bm{\theta}}_{t},t)+\sqrt{2D_{t}}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}={\bm{\theta}}_{t}-{\bm{f}}({\bm{\theta}}_{t},t)+2D_{t}\cdot s({\bm{\theta}}_{t},t)+\sqrt{2D_{t}}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
            Wrap phase: <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}=({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}+\pi)\ \texttt{mod}\ (2\pi)-\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">mod</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}=({\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}+\pi)\ \texttt{mod}\ (2\pi)-\pi</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow t-1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Alg. <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix B More Experimental Results ‣ Kuramoto Orientation Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> outlines the inference procedure for our model. We adopt the SDE formulation by default, but it can be optionally replaced with an ODE solver for improved efficiency by modifying Line 4 to: <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}={\bm{\theta}}_{t}-{\bm{f}}({\bm{\theta}}_{t},t)+D_{t}\cdot s({\bm{\theta}}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}_{t-1}={\bm{\theta}}_{t}-{\bm{f}}({\bm{\theta}}_{t},t)+D_{t}\cdot s({\bm{\theta}}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math>. We use AdamW optimizer with a learning rate of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\mathrm{e}{-}4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\mathrm{e}{-}4</annotation></semantics></math> and apply exponential moving average (EMA) updates with decay rate <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.995" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.995</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.995</annotation></semantics></math>. A single NVIDIA A100 GPU is used for all the training and inference processes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Network Architectures.</span> We use a U-Net architecture following the design of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>, equipped with three self-attention layers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>]</cite>. These are applied at spatial resolutions of <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> for CIFAR-10 and Brodatz, and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>24</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math> for SOCOFing. Timestep conditioning is implemented via sinusoidal positional embeddings. Each block uses group normalization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>]</cite> and GELU activations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> throughout. The same architecture is shared across both our method and SGM for fair comparison.</p>
</div>
