<td id="A2.T5.2.1.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">[<math id="A2.T5.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5e{-}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5e{-}5</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="A2.T5.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>]</td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.1.5.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">[<math id="A2.T5.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5e{-}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5e{-}5</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="A2.T5.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>]</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Schedules of Noise and Coupling Strength.</span> Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ B.1 Implementation Details ‣ Appendix B More Experimental Results ‣ Kuramoto Orientation Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> summarizes the linear schedules for the noise variance <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2D_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2D_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, internal coupling strength <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, and reference phase coupling <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the globally coupled variant, we maintain the relation <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\text{ref}}&gt;2D&gt;K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\text{ref}}&gt;2D&gt;K</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure synchronization toward a reference phase while allowing sufficient noise injection. In the locally coupled variant, we increase the internal coupling strength <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> to compensate for its restricted spatial influence, which is limited to a <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 5</annotation></semantics></math> neighborhood around each pixel. We keep <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\text{ref}}=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\text{ref}}=K</annotation></semantics></math> in this case, since the reference coupling term inherently has a broader impact by acting across the entire image domain. For the SGM baseline, we adopt the VP-SDE formulation with linear variance schedules: <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1\mathrm{e}{-}4,0.1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1\mathrm{e}{-}4,0.1]</annotation></semantics></math> for 100 steps, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1\mathrm{e}{-}4,0.07]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.07</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1\mathrm{e}{-}4,0.07]</annotation></semantics></math> for 300 steps, and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1\mathrm{e}{-}4,0.02]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1\mathrm{e}{-}4,0.02]</annotation></semantics></math> for 1000 steps.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Ablation Study and Alternative Metrics</h3>

<figure id="A2.T6" class="ltx_table">
